tensorplate (0.1.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * V012-F01-T01: add the `tensorplate-apt-source` bootstrap package. It
    installs only the TensorPlate archive keyring and the stable Deb822
    APT source (no runtime packages, no services, no `apt update`).
  * V012-F01-T03: add the `tensorplate` Jetson runtime metapackage
    (arm64 only) so `sudo apt install tensorplate` installs the full
    runtime set, and build/publish `tensorplate-cli` for Ubuntu AMD64
    workstations.
  * V012-F01-T02: publish the signed stable APT repository
    (jammy/main, arm64+amd64) from verified release assets, with
    fail-closed signing/verification against the shipped bootstrap
    keyring and an accumulating pool for future-version discovery.
  * V012-F01-T05: publish the first-party Homebrew tap
    (tensorplate/homebrew-tap) for the macOS Apple Silicon CLI-only
    install, with audit/install/test CI on the tap.
  * V012-F01-T04: document and validate the TensorPlate-ready image
    flow: provisioning runbook, tensorplate-ready-check.sh host
    validation helper, the stock-machine bootstrap fallback, the
    v0.1.1-to-v0.1.2 upgrade plan, and future-version discovery.
  * V012-F01-T06: make the package-manager install the primary public
    story: README two-command install, install-doc restructure with the
    stock-machine bootstrap and AMD64/macOS CLI paths, APT-channel
    verification wording in SECURITY.md, v0.1.2 release notes, and the
    updated support posture.

 -- TensorPlate Contributors <oss@tensorplate.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

tensorplate (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * V01-E14 packaging skeleton: tensorplate-agent, tensorplate-serving,
    tensorplate-observability, tensorplate-cli, and the separately
    installable tensorplate-backend-python-pytorch.
  * systemd units for the agent and observability service. Serving worker
    is supervised by the agent (V01-E09); no `tensorplate-serving.service`.
  * Local-only defaults: agent Unix domain socket, serving worker
    loopback bind, observability in-process / Unix socket transports.
  * `tensorplate doctor` packaging checks for paths, services,
    permissions, backend availability, CUDA / TensorRT / LibTorch /
    Python+PyTorch detection, and the ROS 2 health stub.

 -- TensorPlate Contributors <oss@tensorplate.com>  Wed, 20 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
